cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "plbound: the fixed-false-positive-rate loss of the independence assumption in Gaussian classification, computed with guaranteed error bounds"
abstract: >-
  plbound computes guaranteed enclosures of PL(alpha) = TPR_full(alpha) - TPR_independence(alpha),
  the loss in true positive rate at a fixed false positive rate alpha incurred when a Gaussian
  likelihood-ratio classifier replaces the class covariance matrices by their diagonals. The
  generalized chi-square distribution functions involved are evaluated by midpoint-rule inversion
  of the characteristic function with explicit bounds on aliasing and truncation error and an
  allowance for rounding error, and the bounds are propagated through the quantile that defines the
  threshold. The single file plbound.py is both the Python module and the script that reproduces
  every number, table and figure of the accompanying paper in one run (python plbound.py).
